      "math_academy_id": "q-225068",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(3)$ given below, compute $P(5\\le X<9).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.8153\\,$ | $\\,0.9161\\,$ | $\\,0.9665\\,$ | $\\,0.9881\\,$ | $\\,0.9962\\,$ | $\\,0.9989\\,$ | $\\,0.9997\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X<9) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\})+P(X\\in \\{5,6,7,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(5\\le X<9) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(5\\le X<9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5\\le X<9) & =F(8)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.9962-0.8153 \\\\  & =0.1809.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
